version: 3
metadata:
  name: test_behavior_tree_node
  title: Nav2 behavior-tree recovery, TurtleBot 4 + Nav2, in roqsim (MuJoCo)
  creators:
  - name: Wiest, Samuel
    identifiers: 0009-0002-9215-1238
  - name: Ortega Sainz, Argentina
    identifiers: 0000-0002-3873-4435
  - name: Pasch, Frederik
    identifiers: 0000-0002-2626-1538
  version: 1.0.0
  license: CC-BY-4.0
  keywords: [robotics, navigation, ROS2, mujoco, roqsim, nav2, turtlebot4, behavior-tree, recovery]
  description: |
    Replication of nav2's behavior-tree system test
    (nav2_system_tests/src/behavior_tree/test_behavior_tree_node.cpp, main;
    nav2_system_tests.csv lines 2-8). Where upstream runs an in-process gtest -- a
    BehaviorTreeFactory plus DUMMY action servers (ComputePathToPose, FollowPath, Spin,
    Wait, BackUp) with injectable failure/running ranges, ticked by hand -- this campaign
    runs the REAL nav2 stack (bt_navigator + planner + controller + behavior_server) with
    the stock recovery tree `navigate_to_pose_w_replanning_and_recovery.xml` and drives a
    real NavigateToPose goal. The tree's execution is recorded through /behavior_tree_log
    and analysed for behavior-tree coverage.

    MEANING OF A CELL: one configuration is the runtime analog of one upstream gtest
    case. The blackbox scenario cannot inject per-node failure ranges or tick the tree
    manually, so only the two END-TO-END outcomes upstream produces are ported:

    - bt-all-success  <- TestAllSuccess: a REACHABLE goal (0.0, 2.0). The recovery
      tree's PipelineSequence (ComputePathToPose + FollowPath) succeeds and the tree
      returns SUCCESS. expect_success: true.
    - bt-all-failure  <- TestAllFailure: an UNREACHABLE goal (10.0, 10.0, outside the
      map). ComputePathToPose fails, NavigateRecovery fires the recovery subtree
      (GoalUpdated -> RoundRobin: ClearingActions, Spin, Wait, BackUp), the retries
      exhaust, and the tree returns FAILURE. expect_success: false. This is the case
      that ELICITS the recovery nodes -- the BT-coverage cells show Spin/Wait/BackUp
      actually ticking, which a successful run never reaches.

    NOT PORTED (whitebox/unit -- see readme.md): the XML-parse and ID-extraction tests
    (TestBTXMLFiles, TestWrongBTFormatXML, TestExtractBehaviorTreeID, the duplicate-ID /
    unique-ID registration tests, TestSkipFilesWithMissingID), which need in-process
    factory parsing with no robot involved, and the dummy-server recovery-LOGIC tests
    (TestNavigateSubtreeRecoveries, TestNavigateRecoverySimple, TestNavigateRecoveryComplex,
    TestRecoverySubtreeGoalUpdated), which inject per-server failure/running ranges and
    mid-tick goal updates that a blackbox scenario cannot express. Their recovery
    BEHAVIOUR is the observable bt-all-failure surfaces.

    GRADING: the scenario emits `end` only when the navigate action reports
    STATUS_SUCCEEDED, so bt-all-success passes and bt-all-failure fails (the expected
    upstream verdicts). Behavior-tree coverage is measured per run by
    search/bt_coverage.py:BtCoverage against ground truth and summarised in the
    analysis_run.ipynb "Behavior-tree nodes and coverage" cells. BtCoverage's goal_x/goal_y
    are set to the SUCCESS goal (0.0, 2.0); the bt-all-failure run's `arrived` is 0 by
    design (its outcome is the tree FAILURE, not arrival).
  agents:
  - id: turtlebot4
    configuration_files:
    - files/nav2_stack.launch.py
    - files/nav2_params.yaml
    derived_from: https://github.com/turtlebot/turtlebot4/tree/jazzy
    ros_distro: jazzy
  - id: simulation
    configuration_files:
    - world/nav2.yaml
    derived_from: https://github.com/cps-test-lab/roqsim
    ros_distro: jazzy

configuration:
# --- bt-all-success (runtime analog of upstream TestAllSuccess) ---------------------
# Reachable goal inside the hexagon. PipelineSequence (ComputePathToPose + FollowPath)
# succeeds; the recovery subtree is never triggered; the tree returns SUCCESS.
- name: bt-all-success
  parameters:
  - params_file: files/nav2_params.yaml
  - map_file: environments/hexagon/maps/hexagon.yaml
  - mesh_file: environments/hexagon/3d-mesh/hexagon.stl
  - start_pose:
      position: {x: -2.0, y: -0.5}
  - goal_pose:
      position: {x: 0.0, y: 2.0}
  - nav2_test_id: test_behavior_tree_node/TestAllSuccess
  - expect_success: true
  sim:
    overrides:
      components:
        floorplan:
          mesh: /config/environments/hexagon/3d-mesh/hexagon.stl

# --- bt-all-failure (runtime analog of upstream TestAllFailure) ---------------------
# Unreachable goal far outside the map. ComputePathToPose fails; NavigateRecovery fires
# the recovery subtree (Spin, Wait, BackUp elicited -> positive BT coverage); retries
# exhaust; the tree returns FAILURE.
- name: bt-all-failure
  parameters:
  - params_file: files/nav2_params.yaml
  - map_file: environments/hexagon/maps/hexagon.yaml
  - mesh_file: environments/hexagon/3d-mesh/hexagon.stl
  - start_pose:
      position: {x: -2.0, y: -0.5}
  - goal_pose:
      position: {x: 10.0, y: 10.0}
  - nav2_test_id: test_behavior_tree_node/TestAllFailure
  - expect_success: false
  sim:
    overrides:
      components:
        floorplan:
          mesh: /config/environments/hexagon/3d-mesh/hexagon.stl

execution:
  containers:
    simulation:
      backend: roqsim
      config: world/nav2.yaml
      resources:
        cpu: 1.0
        memory: 6Gi
    sut:
      image: family:robovast
      config_files:
        nav2: files/nav2_params.yaml
      resources:
        cpu: 4
        memory: 6Gi
    scenario:
      image: family:robovast
      resources:
        cpu: 1.75
        memory: 4Gi
  mode: ros2
  runs: 5
  timeout: 240
  scenario_file: behavior_tree.osc
  run_files:
  - "files/*.py"
  - "files/*.yaml"
  - "files/*.xacro"
  - "files/*.xml"
  - "files/nav2/*.py"
  - "files/nav2/*.yaml"
  - "files/models/*.xacro"
  - "environments/hexagon/maps/*"
  - "environments/hexagon/3d-mesh/*"
  - "environments/hexagon/json-ld/*"
  env:
  - PYTHONUNBUFFERED: "1"
  local:
    gui:
      parameter_overrides:
      - use_rviz: "True"

results_processing:
  postprocessing:
  - rosbags_tf_to_csv:
      frames: all
      require: [base_link, odom, nav2_turtlebot4_base_link_gt]
  - rosbags_action_to_csv:
      action: follow_waypoints
  - rosbags_action_to_csv:
      action: navigate_to_pose
  - rosbags_to_csv:
      topics: [/collision]
  - rosbags_nav2bt_to_csv
  - nav2_bt_tree:
      bt_xml: files/navigate_to_pose_w_replanning_and_recovery.xml
  # goal_x/goal_y match the SUCCESS goal (0.0, 2.0). The bt-all-failure run's `arrived`
  # is 0 by design: its outcome is the tree FAILURE after recovery, not arrival.
  - search/bt_coverage.py:BtCoverage:
      goal_x: 0.0
      goal_y: 2.0
      arrival_radius: 0.6
  - rosbags_costmap_to_csv:
      topics: [/map, /global_costmap/costmap, /local_costmap/costmap]

visualization:
  config:
    panels:
    - parameters: {title: Scenario parameters, height: "30%"}
    - world: {title: World configuration, height: "15%"}
    - map2d:
        title: Map
        map: {param: map_file}
        markers:
        - {kind: pose, param: start_pose, label: start, color: "#60a5fa"}
        - {kind: pose, param: goal_pose, label: goal, color: "#ef4444"}
  results:
    run_view:
      panels:
      - nav2_behavior_tree:
          title: Nav2 Behavior Tree
          position: {anchor: top-left, width: 320, height: "calc(50% - 44px)"}
          minimizable: true
      - scenario_tree:
          title: Scenario
          position: {anchor: bottom-left, width: 320, height: "calc(50% - 44px)"}
          minimizable: true
          source: {table: behaviors}
      - costmap:
          title: Nav2 Costmap
          position: {anchor: top-right, width: 320, height: 550}
          minimizable: true
          layers:
            map: {topic: /map}
            global: {topic: /global_costmap/costmap}
            local: {topic: /local_costmap/costmap}
            poses: {table: poses}
      - log:
          title: Run log
          position: {anchor: bottom-center, width: "calc(100% - 680px)", height: 380}
          minimizable: true
          minimized: true
      - vega:
          title: Metrics
          position: {anchor: bottom-right, width: 320, height: 380}
          minimizable: true
          source: {table: poses, filter: {frame: base_link}, decimate_hz: 2}
          vega_lite:
            resolve: {scale: {x: shared}}
            spacing: 8
            transform:
            - {calculate: "datum['position.x']", as: px}
            - {calculate: "datum['position.y']", as: py}
            - {calculate: "datum['orientation.yaw']", as: yaw}
            - window:
              - {op: lag, field: px, as: px0}
              - {op: lag, field: py, as: py0}
              - {op: lag, field: timestamp, as: t0}
              sort: [{field: timestamp}]
            - filter: "isValid(datum.t0)"
            - filter: "datum.timestamp - datum.t0 > 0"
            - calculate: >
                sqrt(pow(datum.px - datum.px0, 2) + pow(datum.py - datum.py0, 2))
                / (datum.timestamp - datum.t0)
              as: speed
            - window: [{op: mean, field: speed, as: speed_avg}]
              frame: [-9, 0]
              sort: [{field: timestamp}]
            vconcat:
            - height: 150
              encoding:
                x: {field: timestamp, type: quantitative, axis: null}
                y: {field: speed_avg, type: quantitative, title: "speed [m/s]"}
              layer:
              - mark: {type: line, opacity: 0.25, strokeWidth: 1}
                encoding: {y: {field: speed, type: quantitative}}
              - mark: {type: line, strokeWidth: 1.5}
            - height: 120
              transform: [{fold: [px, py, yaw], as: [series, value]}]
              mark: {type: line, strokeWidth: 1.5}
              encoding:
                x: {field: timestamp, type: quantitative, title: "t [s]"}
                y: {field: value, type: quantitative, title: pose}
                color: {field: series, type: nominal, legend: {title: null, orient: top}}
    explorer:
      notebooks:
      - Analysis:
          run: analysis/analysis_run.ipynb
          config: analysis/analysis_config.ipynb
          campaign: analysis/analysis_campaign.ipynb
      - Resource Usage:
          run: analysis/resource_usage_run.ipynb
          config: analysis/resource_usage_config.ipynb
